    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0147" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3754: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Poole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 29, 3:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>804. The following is being sent to Paris.</p>
                <p>Number 26, January 28, 5 p.m. I received last night from the Provisional
                    Government a six hundred [<hi rendition="#italic">six?</hi>] page note, to the
                    effect <pb facs="0148" n="36" xml:id="pg36"/> that it is both practically and
                    morally impossible to accept the proposition of a conference of Russian factions
                    which would include the Bolsheviki. The British Commissioner is telegraphing a
                    complete English translation<anchor n="37" xml:id="d25-f1"/> to the British
                    peace mission in Paris and asking that a copy be furnished to you. The French
                    Embassy has telegraphed a summary to the Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
